      "spam": false,
      "value": "Testing some more, it feels like the nudge and forward motion in general is a lot easier to control if I make sure I raise my thumb up far enough.  Many users like myself never actually take it off the pad entirely, and is hard to do even when thinking about it, but now over and over I tried it just barely above the pad... so it felt like I had a sliver of space between it and my thumb... and it still kept moving forward.  If I raised it further, no problem.  But I had no idea that it could react to touch so light I wasn't even aware of it.  This might be a big reason why some of us are having issues figuring it out.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
