  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2018-02-25T12:25:48.836Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Okay so I finally figured out why it feels so glitchy for me, and how it might be fixed, so I'd be able to use the new controls without getting sick. Or rather how others who are sensitive can avoid this and I can avoid having to learn to lift my thumb fast and high enough to navigate efficiently.\n\nIt comes down to having the normal grip where your thumb lays across the pad at all times. Those that don't use gestures aren't used to having to hover it above the bad, or rest it beneath. It's so unusual a position for me that I didn't even realize I was brushing against it, so that when I'm nudging forward at the top of the pad, it feels normal when it does just nudge me, but when I give just a bit more soft contact after the hard press and it keeps going, then I wasn't able to notice what was going on.\n\nIMO the very top should just be nudge. When you make brush against that area it ideally shouldn't have any other effect on motion. Very near the top, you could have it as it is now, and I could easily learn to just tap the top without moving down further. This way I could still adjust speed easily if I wanted to have motion without holding on to it, which I personally might not choose to do but I see how it could be handy.\n\nAnd then you still have most of the pad to do your gestures and such.\n\nDoes this make any sense? At the very least it should be made clear that people need to adjust their grip. And if you want to nudge forward, which I do constantly when sitting down in while playing vrchat, then you have to make very quick, clear motions at the top.",
